---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Tiered Storage"
  description="Decouple compute from storage with S3, GCS, and MinIO tiered offloading and local NVMe caching in Krabka."
  currentSlug="/docs/tiered-storage"
>
  <div class="space-y-6">
    <div class="border-b border-white/10 pb-4">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-white sm:text-4xl">Tiered Storage Architecture</h1>
      <p class="text-gray-400 mt-2 text-base">
        Cloud object storage offloading via <code class="font-mono text-krab-300">krabka-remote-storage</code> and <code class="font-mono text-krab-300">krabka-object-store</code>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-sm text-gray-300">
      <p>
        Tiered storage decouples high-throughput real-time streaming from historical data retention. Log segments rolled on local NVMe SSDs are sealed and asynchronously offloaded to Amazon S3, Google Cloud Storage, or MinIO.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">Remote Log Metadata Manager (RLMM)</h2>
      <p>
        Metadata for offloaded segments is stored durably in the internal compacted topic <code class="font-mono text-krab-300 text-xs">__remote_log_metadata</code> (<code class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-200">krabka-remote-storage-topic</code>), ensuring zero external catalog database dependencies.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
